{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4f62d814d802df1","type":"tool_result","content":"/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:4:summary: Added SUPERSEDE_LOOKBACK config field (default 7) wired from application struct through factory into CreateTaskExecutor, replaced literal 7 placeholder, added startup guard for non-positive values, created argument-parse test, rewrote period-token-semantics.md to scan-and-collapse contract, added CHANGELOG feat entry, and created supersede scenario\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:26:Expose the supersede look-back bound K as a controller env var (`SUPERSEDE_LOOKBACK`, default 7), wired from the application config through the factory into the create-task executor (replacing the literal `7` placeholder from prompt 2). Rewrite `docs/period-token-semantics.md` to the scan-and-collapse contract, add the CHANGELOG entry, and update the supersede scenario coverage.\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:33:Read `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` for CHANGELOG entry format (prefix required, specific, one bullet per logical change).\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:88:6. **Add the CHANGELOG entry** to `/workspace/CHANGELOG.md`. If a `## Unreleased` section does not exist, add one immediately below the top header block (above `## v0.1.1`). Add a single `feat:` bullet describing the change; the word `scan` MUST appear (AC grep target). Example:\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:115:- Per `changelog-guide.md`: the CHANGELOG entry has a `feat:` prefix, is specific, and is a single logical bullet.\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:148:CHANGELOG (spec AC):\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:151:cd /workspace && grep -n 'scan' CHANGELOG.md\n/workspace/prompts/completed/009-spec-004-wire-lookback-env-docs-changelog.md:168:Expected: exit 0; the lookback default + override parse tests pass; the doc/CHANGELOG/scenario greps above satisfy the ACs; all existing tests still pass.\n---changelog-guide---\n27:## Unreleased\n30:- fix: Remove stale Docker container before starting a new executor run\n35:- fix: Fix WaiterUntil to handle equal times correctly\n41:**Applies when**: a CHANGELOG.md edit inserts content above the `# Changelog` title, modifies the SemVer preamble bullets (MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH), or places a `## Unreleased` / `## vX.Y.Z` section inside (rather than after) the preamble block.\n42:**Enforcement**: `scripts/rule-checks.sh` (checks `# Changelog` is first content; flags any `## Unreleased`/`## vX.Y.Z` before the preamble block)\n48:## Unreleased\n63:## Unreleased\n69:- **Header is frozen**: everything from the start of the file to the FIRST `##` heading (the `# Changelog` title, the \"All notable changes...\" line, the SemVer link, and the MAJOR/MINOR/PATCH bullets) MUST NOT be moved, deleted, or have anything inserted above or inside it. Insert `## Unreleased` (or any version section) immediately AFTER the last header line — never before any header line. If the header is incomplete, restore it; never leave it partial.\n70:- `## Unreleased` on feature branches — never a version number\n72:- Newest version first — `## Unreleased` goes directly above the highest `## vX.Y.Z`\n80:**Applies when**: a bullet under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md does not start with one of the recognised conventional prefixes (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `chore:`, `perf:`).\n81:**Enforcement**: judgment (regex over `## Unreleased` bullets: `^- ([a-z]+:)` first token must be in the allowed prefix set)\n88:## Unreleased\n97:## Unreleased\n103:Every `## Unreleased` entry must start with a conventional prefix:\n108:| `fix:` | Bug fix | Patch |\n117:## Every Source-Changing PR Needs an Unreleased Entry (REQUIRED)\n122:**Applies when**: the repo root contains a `CHANGELOG.md`, the PR changes at least one non-vendored file, and the PR-HEAD `CHANGELOG.md` has no `-` bullet under its `## Unreleased` heading (the section is absent or empty).\n123:**Enforcement**: script (`scripts/rule-checks.sh`) — diff-scoped only; when ≥1 non-vendored file changed and `CHANGELOG.md` exists at the repo root, scan the `## Unreleased` section of the PR-HEAD `CHANGELOG.md` for a `-`/`*` bullet and flag when none is present. Deterministic state-check — does not depend on the review model executing a judgment step (so it fires reliably even on a weak review model). Trade-offs: no trivial-diff waiver (a comment/whitespace-only change still needs a bullet), and a `## Unreleased` already populated by an earlier unreleased merge suppresses the flag.\n124:**Why**: In an `autoRelease: true` repo the release agent renames `## Unreleased` → `## vX.Y.Z` after merge. A PR merged with an empty `## Unreleased` makes the release agent no-op — the change reaches `master` but never ships to consumers. Requiring one bullet per source-changing PR is the forcing function that keeps every merge releasable. Gate on `CHANGELOG.md` presence alone, not `autoRelease` — manual-release repos also need the section current for the human releaser.\n130:# ## Unreleased stays empty → after merge the release agent has\n137:## Unreleased\n143:- Every PR that changes a non-vendored file in a repo with a `CHANGELOG.md` adds at least one `## Unreleased` bullet (with a conventional prefix per the rule above).\n144:- Deterministic state-check — the check reads the PR-HEAD `## Unreleased` section, not the diff, so it needs no base-branch resolution and fires regardless of the review model. It intentionally has **no** trivial-diff waiver.\n145:- Not a version-string bump — the entry is a bullet under `## Unreleased`, never a manifest edit (see § Version Alignment Is Release-Time).\n165:❌ `- fix: refactor` — what was refactored?\n171:❌ `- fix: fix bug` — which bug?\n172:✅ `- fix: Fix NormalizeFilenames number conflict on non-standard filename format`\n174:## Merge Conflicts in Unreleased\n176:Multiple feature branches writing to `## Unreleased` will conflict. Resolution: keep both bullet lists, remove conflict markers.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9412ecfd5e7d447b","session_id":"c245cf91-e27d-42c2-b8e2-b86a59610663","uuid":"85937f67-c262-484d-9121-08e7236645ef","timestamp":"2026-08-27T18:30:04.390Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Create prompts from spec 005"}
