tinct commit message containing `reopen terminal task`, positive/negative commit-message unit specs, `CHANGELOG.md` `## Unreleased` + `fix:` bullet, and the terminal-status definition section in `docs/controller-design.md`.\n- **No scenario prompt**: the spec explicitly declares \"NO new E2E scenario\" and all branches are reachable via the `fakeGit` counterfeiter harness — the four-condition scenario test fails on condition (a).\n\n**Key constraints repeated in each prompt:** frozen change site, frozen sentinel + `\"title path %s occupied\"` message shape, frozen terminal set (exactly `completed`/`aborted`, not `done`), fail-closed invariant (no parse-failure-to-write path), single `ReadFile` per create, reuse of `result.ExtractFrontmatter` + `parseTaskFrontmatter`, no new config/knobs/frontmatter markers, no content carried forward from the terminal file, no commit.\n\n**Docs referenced in `<context>`** (in-container `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/...` paths): `go-patterns.md`, `go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-glog-guide.md`, `changelog-guide.md`, `definition-of-done.md`; project docs: `docs/controller-design.md` (background in prompt 1, edit target in prompt 2), `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n**Verification design note:** the daemon environment has `.git` masked (`git status` → `fatal: not a git repository`), so I deliberately did NOT emit bare `git` commands in `<verification>` — the AC's `git diff` evidence for the unmodified collision contexts is proxied by grep counts (`grep -c '...To(BeTrue())'` expects exactly 2, and the stale-comment grep expects no match), with the git-diff confirmation noted as operator-side at merge. All `kubectl`/Rung-3 steps stay in the spec's operator-executable rung, not the prompts.\n\n**Open questions embedded as `<!-- OPEN QUESTION -->` comments for the human reviewer:**\n- Prompt 1: `writeTaskFile` gains `reopened`/`priorStatus` params that are declared-but-unused this prompt (per the spec's mandated plumbing split); flag if you'd rather merge the two prompts.\n- Prompt 2: the full reopen commit-message form `\"[agent-task-controller] reopen terminal task <id>\"` is my choice mirroring the existing `\"[agent-task-controller] create task <id>\"` — the spec only freezes the `reopen terminal task` substring.\n\nSuggest running `/audit-prompt prompts/1-spec-005-terminal-reopen-decision.md` and `/audit-prompt prompts/2-spec-005-reopen-observability.md` to validate before approving.","usage":{"total_tokens":0,"tool_uses":41,"duration_ms":301434},"uuid":"db438264-0de5-4cec-896a-47842a026cab","session_id":"c245cf91-e27d-42c2-b8e2-b86a59610663"}
