ugh, with inlined verified helper signatures\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered, specific, with exact paths, signatures, and old→new code\n- [x] `<constraints>` present, faithfully copied from spec, includes \"Do NOT commit\"\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable commands (but one self-inconsistent check — see Critical #2)\n- [x] All paths resolve inside the container (repo-relative; `/workspace` is the mount; coding-doc + module-cache paths are container paths; no host-absolute/`~/` paths)\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` under masked git — daemon log shows `hideGit=true` (via `--set` arg), `.git` is a `/dev/null` char device; the prompt's verification is grep/make-only and explicitly defers the `git diff` AC evidence to the operator side\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` (`make test`, `grep -c`, `grep -n`, `make precommit` only)\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (in-progress dir is empty)\n- [x] Filename uses allowed single-digit multi-prompt ordering prefix (`1-spec-005-...`), not a dark-factory global number\n- [x] Filename reflects primary change (terminal-status dedup decision)\n- [x] Status `draft`, only `spec`/`status`/`created` in frontmatter, canonical full-slug `spec` value\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed in requirements — rows 1 (transient non-404 → Req 1a + existing AC5 test), 2 (unparseable/missing status → Req 1b/1c + 5-case table), 3 (terminal body overwritten → Req 7 byte-identity + not-contains), 4 (Kafka redelivery → Req 7 replay-idempotency), 7 (write fails → unchanged \"git write error\" context), 8 (title date advances → Non-goal, out of scope)\n- [x] Security section addressed — fail-closed invariant enforced as a hard constraint (\"no code path where a parse failure results in a write\"), terminal-only overwrite preserved, `resolveCreateTaskRelPath` untouched\n- [x] External calls have timeout/cancellation — N/A (no new I/O; the status decision reuses the existing coll