tor-side at merge.\n\n**Open questions embedded as `<!-- OPEN QUESTION -->` comments for the human reviewer:**\n- Prompt 1: `writeTaskFile` gains `reopened`/`priorStatus` params that are declared-but-unused this prompt (per the spec's mandated plumbing split); flag if you'd rather merge the two prompts.\n- Prompt 2: the full reopen commit-message form `\"[agent-task-controller] reopen terminal task <id>\"` is the creator's choice mirroring the existing `\"[agent-task-controller] create task <id>\"` — the spec only freezes the `reopen terminal task` substring.\n\n## Audit Findings\n\n### prompts/1-spec-005-terminal-reopen-decision.md\n\n# Prompt Audit Report: Terminal-status dedup decision in create-task\n\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-005-terminal-reopen-decision.md`\n**Score**: 6/10\n**Status**: Needs Improvement — two verification-correctness defects must be fixed before approval (one empirically proven against the repo's own lint toolchain)\n\n## DoD Checklist\n\n- [x] `<summary>` present, largely plain-language (minor jargon nit, see Recommendations)\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state and why\n- [x] `<context>` present, thorough, with inlined verified helper signatures\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered, specific, with exact paths, signatures, and old→new code\n- [x] `<constraints>` present, faithfully copied from spec, includes \"Do NOT commit\"\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable commands (but one self-inconsistent check — see Critical #2)\n- [x] All paths resolve inside the container (repo-relative; `/workspace` is the mount; coding-doc + module-cache paths are container paths; no host-absolute/`~/` paths)\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` under masked git — daemon log shows `hideGit=true` (via `--set` arg), `.git` is a `/dev/null` char device; the prompt's verification is grep/make-only and explicitly defers the `git diff` AC evidence to the operator side\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` (`make test`, `grep -c`, `grep -n`, `make precommit` only)\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (in-progress dir is empty)\n- [x] Filename uses allowed single-digit multi-prompt ordering prefix (`1-spec-005-...`), not a dark-factory global number\n- [x] Filename reflects primary change (terminal-status dedup decision)\n- [x] Status `draft`, only `spec`/`status`/`created` in frontmatter, canonical full-slug `spec` value\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed in requirements — rows 1 (transient non-404 → Req 1a + existing AC5 test), 2 (unparseable/missing status → Req 1b/1c + 5-case table), 3 (terminal body overwritten → Req 7 byte-identity + not-contains), 4 (Kafka redelivery → Req 7 replay-idempotency), 7 (write fails → unchanged \"git write error\" context), 8 (title date advances → Non-goal, out of scope)\n- [x] Security section addressed — fail-closed invariant enforced as a hard constraint (\"no code path where a parse failure results in a write\"), terminal-only overwrite preserved, `resolveCreateTaskRelPath` untouched\n- [x] External calls have timeout/cancellation — N/A (no new I/O; the status decision reuses the existing collision read; `ctx` already threaded)\n- [x] New constants through library validators — N/A/covered: `completed`/`aborted` are in-package string comparisons (no external validator); the `yaml.Unmarshal` / `ExtractFrontmatter` parse boundaries ARE exercised by the 5-case ambiguous table (incl. case 2 `status: [` which I verified fails yaml only after ExtractFrontmatter succeeds)\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in requirements/verification\n- [x] No cross-repo writes (no clone/push/gh)\n- [x] Container-autonomous (no kubectl/deploy/\"trigger a PR\"/observe-pods; no operator/agent step split)\n- [x] Sibling entry points covered — `checkTitlePathFree` and `ErrTaskAlreadyExists` production are unique to `task_create_task_executor.go`; `NewCreateTaskExecutor` is constructed only at `pkg/factory/factory.go:43`. Single entry point, no sibling gate to bypass\n- [ ] **Failure-mode row 5 (concurrent same-title, different-identifier) has no matching requirement** in prompt 1 or sibling prompt 2 — see Recommendation 1\n\n## Documentation Placement\n\n- [x] No inlined reusable cross-project patterns — the inlined `checkTitlePathFree` body is change-specific and reuses existing helpers; no pattern collision detected (errors.Wrapf 92 uses in pkg/, prompt uses errors.Wrapf; Ginkgo in 32 files, prompt uses Ginkgo; counterfeiter mocks reused, not hand-written)\n- [x] Project docs referenced in `<context>` (`docs/controller-design.md` — verified the status/phase merge section exists)\n- [x] Coding-plugin docs referenced and all five exist (`go-patterns.md`, `go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-glog-guide.md`, `definition-of-done.md`)\n- [x] Domain knowledge (terminal-status rule) correctly deferred to prompt 2's `docs/controller-design.md` update\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `checkTitlePathFree` lines 95-123 | `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go` | Verified / Correct |\n| `NewCreateTaskExecutor` doc 29-36, call site 82-85 | same | Verified / Correct |\n| `isNotFoundReadError` line 192 | same | Verified / Correct |\n| `writeTaskFile` line 128; `buildCreateTaskContent` | same | Verified / Correct |\n| Imports `strings`, `errors`, `glog`, `result`, `task` | same (lines 11, 15, 18, 22, 25) | Verified / Correct |\n| `parseTaskFrontmatter` 126, `marshalFileContent` 152 | `pkg/command/task_increment_frontmatter_executor.go` | Verified / Correct |\n| `ExtractFrontmatter` 368 (366-385 claimed) | `pkg/result/result_writer.go` | Verified / Correct |\n| `TaskFrontmatter map[string]interface{}` (mod line 16), `String(key)` (mod line 144) | `github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.83.0` (version confirmed in go.mod line 6) | Verified / Correct |\n| `ErrTaskAlreadyExists` at `command/task/errors.go:18` | agent module | Verified / Correct |\n| Test harness claims (`package command_test`, mocks, BeforeEach 404, collision contexts 163/212, stale comment 214-215, `buildCmdObj`) | `pkg/command/task_create_task_executor_test.go` | Verified / Correct |\n| Mock shapes (`ReadFileReturnsOnCall`, `ReadFileCallCount`, `AtomicWriteAndCommitPushArgsForCall` 4-tuple) | `mocks/git_client.go` (lines 613, 584, 232) | Verified / Correct |\n| `DescribeTable`/`Entry` style | `pkg/command/period_token_ranking_test.go` | Verified / Correct |\n\nAll line numbers and signatures check out exactly. The five ambiguous/unreadable test fixtures all behave as claimed (verified `ExtractFrontmatter` + `yaml.Unmarshal` outcomes for each).\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, ...)` — never `fmt.Errorf` (both `fmt.Errorf` mentions in the prompt are prohibitions, not inlined code) | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant |\n| No `context.Background()` in `pkg/` | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant |\n| Ginkgo/Gomega external test package, reuse existing harness | `go-testing-guide.md` | Compliant |\n| Reuses existing helpers, no invented primitives | `go-composition.md` | Compliant |\n| No test-only package-level mutable state introduced | `go-composition.md` | Compliant |\n| funlen/nestif headroom — new `checkTitlePathFree` max nesting 2, ~30 lines | `go-precommit.md` | Compliant (would pass) |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n\n- [x] No opt-out flag, config field, env var, or tunable terminal list (constraints explicitly forbid all)\n- [x] The `reopened bool, priorStatus string` plumbing is **spec-demanded**, not prompt-writer scope creep — the spec's Suggested Decomposition assigns \"plumb the reopen fact out to the write path\" to prompt 1 and observability to prompt 2. No removal needed.\n\n## Critical Issues\n\n### Critical 1 — Requirement 3 mandates a state that fails `make lint` (unparam); the prompt's claim \"the linter does not flag them\" is false, and `<verification>` requires `make precommit` exit 0\n\n**Line 192.** The prompt instructs the executor to add `reopened bool, priorStatus string` to `writeTaskFile` and leave them **declared but unused**, asserting: *\"Go permits unused function parameters; the linter does not flag them.\"*\n\nThis is **empirically false for this repo**. `.golangci.yml` enables `unparam` (excluded only for `_test.go`), and `make precommit` → `check` → `lint` runs golangci-lint v2.13.1 with it. I applied Requirements 1-3 verbatim to a copy of the repo and ran the repo's real `make lint`:\n\n```\npkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go:135:2: writeTaskFile - reopened is unused (unparam)\npkg/command/task_create_task_executor.go:136:2: writeTaskFile - priorStatus is unused (unparam)\nexit status 1\nmake: *** [Makefile.precommit:44: lint] Error 1\n```\n\nThe copy compiled and the existing tests passed, so these two findings are purely the prompt's mandated state. An executor following Requirement 3 verbatim will fail the `<verification>`'s `make precommit`, and will be forced to invent a workaround (`_ = reopened`) that Requirement 3 explicitly forbids. (I also confirmed the \"result reopened is always false\" unparam finding from my stub is an artifact of my minimal reproduction — the full prompt body has a `return true, ...` branch, so it will not fire in the real implementation.)\n\n**Fix** (validated: after applying the below consumption, `make lint` returns clean): replace the sentence at line 192 —\n\n> The two new parameters are declared but not yet consumed — the observability that distinguishes a reopen (unconditional INFO log + distinct commit message) is specified by the follow-up prompt in this spec (Desired Behavior 5). Go permits unused function parameters; the linter does not flag them.\n\nwith:\n\n> The two new parameters MUST be referenced in the function body: the repo's `.golangci.yml` enables `unparam`, which flags declared-but-unused parameters in non-test code, and `make precommit` runs `make lint` over it (verified — `writeTaskFile - reopened is unused (unparam)`). Do NOT ship the observability here (the frozen `create-task: reopening terminal task` INFO log and the `reopen terminal task` commit message remain the follow-up prompt's scope); instead consume both params with a debug-only reference immediately before the `buildCreateTaskContent` call, which satisfies unparam and uses neither frozen substring so the follow-up prompt's grep ACs are unaffected:\n>\n> ```go\n> if reopened {\n>     glog.V(3).Infof(\"create-task: terminal reopen signal (prior status %s)\", priorStatus)\n> }\n> ```\n>\n> Keep the content, commit message, and the existing `glog.V(2).Infof(\"create-task: created task file at ...\")` line unchanged.\n\n(Alternative, cleanest resolution: the `<context>` OPEN QUESTION already floats merging prompts 1+2 — merging removes the declared-but-unused state entirely. If the observability ships atomically with the decision, the lint failure disappears and the frozen substrings are still correctly scoped.)\n\n### Critical 2 — `<verification>` \"Expect exactly 2\" is self-inconsistent with Requirement 7; the count will never be 2 after the mandated tests are added\n\n**Lines 258-261.** The verification runs:\n\n```\ncd /workspace && grep -c 'Expect(errors.Is(err, task.ErrTaskAlreadyExists)).To(BeTrue())' pkg/command/task_create_task_executor_test.go\n```\nExpect exactly `2` (the two pre-existing collision contexts' sentinel assertions, unmodified).\n\nRequirement 7 mandates new tests that assert the same sentinel with the same natural Gomega form: the non-terminal `DescribeTable` body, the ambiguous/unreadable `DescribeTable` body, and the replay-idempotency second-handle assertion. Each adds a textual occurrence of the exact grepped string. After the prompt's own tests are added the file contains **5** occurrences (2 pre-existing at lines 190/229 + 3 new), not 2. The check cannot produce its documented result, and a literal executor either reports a false verification failure or \"fixes\" it by contorting the new tests. `grep -c` over the whole file cannot distinguish \"pre-existing assertions unmodified\" from \"new assertions added\".\n\n**Fix** — scope the grep to the two adjacent, frozen collision contexts (Requirement 6 freezes them in place, so the anchors are stable). Replace lines 258-261 with:\n\n```\ncd /workspace && sed -n '/Context(\"title path already occupied (collision)\")/,/Context(\"transient git-rest read error\")/p' pkg/command/task_create_task_executor_test.go | grep -c 'Expect(errors.Is(err, task.ErrTaskAlreadyExists)).To(BeTrue())'\n```\nExpect exactly `2` (the two pre-existing collision contexts' sentinel assertions, unmodified). New test `Context` blocks added elsewhere in the file fall outside this range.\n\n(Simpler alternative: drop the count check entirely — `make precommit` behaviorally enforces both contexts' assertions, and the existing `grep -n 'must not consult frontmatter'` → no-match check already proves the comment edit. The spec's own AC evidence for \"pre-existing specs unmodified\" is `git diff`, which is operator-side by design.)\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Spec failure-mode row 5 (two concurrent same-title, different-identifier creates) has no matching requirement in either prompt** (severity: Recommendation, not Critical — the spec explicitly documents last-write-wins as the *designed, reversible* outcome, and true concurrency is not unit-testable with the fakeGit harness). Add one proxy test: reopen a terminal file, then issue a create for the same title with a *different* `task_identifier` and assert `ErrTaskAlreadyExists` + write count unchanged. This locks the row's \"next sweep suppresses further writes because the file is now non-terminal\" tail, which the current replay-idempotency test (same identifier) does not cover.\n\n2. **Summary jargon nit (line 12)**: bullet 2 uses the sentinel name `ErrTaskAlreadyExists` verbatim. The summary guidance asks for plain language for the human reviewer — suggest \"is still dropped with the existing 'task already exists' failure\". Minor.\n\n3. **Verification count-2 context (Requirement 7)**: the \"completed → reopen\" test asserts `ReadFileCallCount() == 1`, which depends on `supersedePriorRecurringTask` being a no-op for the test command (no `created_by`). This is correct as written, but it is a silent coupling — a one-line note in the test that the single-read lock holds only because the command is not supersede-eligible would prevent a future executor from \"helpfully\" adding `created_by` and breaking the assertion.\n\n## Strengths\n\n- Every code reference is accurate — I verified all line numbers, signatures, mock shapes, module symbols (including `TaskFrontmatter.String` semantics at `agent_task-frontmatter.go:144`), and the go.mod module version `v0.83.0`.\n- The five ambiguous/unreadable test fixtures are each correct against the actual `ExtractFrontmatter` + `parseTaskFrontmatter` behavior (verified the `status: [` YAML-fails-after-delimiters claim).\n- The two-prompt decomposition is clean and the cross-prompt dependency is explicit and verifiable (prompt 2 greps `reopened bool` before starting); the OPEN QUESTION in `<context>` flags the one genuinely awkward seam.\n- The single-`ReadFile` lock is made observable by design (`ReadFileReturns`, not `ReadFileReturnsOnCall`), the fail-closed invariant is enforced as a hard constraint, and the security bounding properties from the spec are preserved.\n\n## Summary\n\nStructurally excellent prompt: all references verified, spec constraints and failure modes faithfully carried, tests comprehensive, observability correctly deferred to the sibling prompt. However, two verification-correctness defects block approval: Requirement 3 mandates declared-but-unused parameters that fail the repo's own `make lint` (empirically proven — the prompt's \"the linter does not flag them\" claim is false), and the `<verification>` sentinel-count check is self-inconsistent with the tests Requirement 7 mandates. Both have exact find/replace fixes above; once applied (and with Recommendation 1 optionally added), this is an exemplary prompt.\n\nNote: the environment's local `golangci-lint` binary is v1 and cannot parse the repo's v2 config, so I validated Critical 1 using the exact tool the repo's `make lint` invokes (`go run github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@v2.13.1`), against a faithful copy of the repo with Requirements 1-3 applied — the copy compiled and passed its existing tests, isolating the two unparam findings as the prompt's mandated state.\n\n### prompts/2-spec-005-reopen-observability.md\n\n# Prompt Audit Report: Reopen observability for create-task terminal reopen\n\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-005-reopen-observability.md`\n**Score**: 9/10\n**Status**: Excellent\n\n## DoD Checklist\n- [x] `<summary>` present and plain-language — 6 bullets, no file paths/struct names, each an observable outcome\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state — \"operator-greppable in exactly the two places the spec freezes\", 2 sentences, references only frozen substrings\n- [x] `<context>` present — read-first list with specific paths, coding-plugin docs, and a fail-loud dependency gate on prompt 1\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered and specific — 7 requirements, exact paths, code snippets, positive+negative assertions\n- [x] `<constraints>` present — frozen substrings, unconditional-log requirement, no-config/no-marker invariants, error-wrapping rule, do-not-commit, do-not-kubectl\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable command — `make test` iterative, grep AC checks, `make precommit` at end\n- [x] All paths repo-relative — `/workspace` prefix is the mounted repo root; `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/*.md` paths are the documented container-baked coding-plugin location (verified present), not host mounts\n- [x] No bar